  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Amerisourcebergen Drug has $4.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company received 289,045 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $15.7K, and obligations fell 38.9% year over year. Obligations have varied across recent fiscal years: FY21 was $2.1B, FY22 was $2B, FY23 was $4.4B, FY24 was $6.1B, FY25 was $7.4B, and FY26 is $4.5B to date. The Department of Defense is the leading buyer with $4.5B in obligations this year. The Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Justice follow with $639K and $28K respectively. Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing is the largest NAICS market with $3.1B in obligations, followed by Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers with $1.5B and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing with $639K. All figures here are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
